# Manuscript under review.
#
# The .tex and compiled PDF are deliberately not tracked. iThenticate, which
# journals reach through Crossref Similarity Check, crawls public repositories:
# a manuscript published here matches itself at submission and produces a
# similarity report an editor has to unpick before reading the paper.
#
# Nothing in the reproducibility claim depends on these files. The simulation
# harness, the figure scripts and the test suite are what regenerate every
# number, and they remain tracked.
# Match by extension, not by name. The two lines below previously named one
# specific file, and the compiled PDF actually sent to the editor is called
# Aggarwal_EstimatorConfound_JEDM.pdf, so it was tracked by nothing and a
# single "git add -A" would have published the manuscript.
# Figures live in paper/figures/ and stay tracked; the class file, bibliography
# and style file are not manuscript text.
paper/*.tex
paper/*.pdf
